# Code owners — the files that decide whether a submission is acceptable.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, and it is not general hygiene.
#
# `addon-pr.yml` says of itself that the gate must not be modifiable by what it
# is gating, and runs every check from the base revision for exactly that
# reason. That holds for the scripts. It does NOT hold for the workflow file,
# because on a `pull_request` event GitHub executes the workflow YAML from the
# pull request's own merge commit, not from the base. So a submission that adds
# `addons/x/**` and replaces `addon-pr.yml` with a job of the same name that
# exits 0 produces a green required check, and stage 1 — which refuses a patch
# touching anything outside `addons/<id>/` — never runs, because stage 1 is
# inside the file that was replaced.
#
# What that does and does not get an attacker: a forged passing check on a bad
# add-on. It gains no CI privilege (the job holds `contents: read` and fork
# secrets are absent), and GitHub shows the `.github/` change in the diff. So
# the exposure is a maintainer trusting the check over the file list.
#
# This file makes that require a maintainer's review. The standing rule it
# encodes, which matters more than the mechanism: AN ADD-ON SUBMISSION HAS NO
# REASON TO TOUCH ANY OF THESE PATHS, so one that does is refused on sight
# rather than read.
#
# Enabling "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection for `main`
# is what gives this file effect. Without that setting it is advisory.

# The review machinery itself.
/.github/                       @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe
/scripts/                       @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe

# The licensing and contribution terms a submission is accepted under.
/LICENSING.md                   @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe
/MAINTAINERS.md                 @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe
/LICENSE                        @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe
/NOTICE                         @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe

# The publisher keys. An add-on's signature is worth whatever this file is.
/publisher-keys.json            @zephyrnova @dxnn @BarryJRowe

# Deliberately NOT listed: `addons/`. That is where submissions go, and
# requiring a code-owner review there would say nothing — every submission
# needs a maintainer's review already, and the point of this file is to
# distinguish the submission from the rules it is judged by.
